 "text": "HUNTING LAB, 2026-10-09\n16 new ways to catch moves, each a complete trade, tested on the whole US market 2021-10-12 to 2026-10-09 (collapsed stocks included), 0.8% cost. Rules fixed in advance (the build-up version is chosen on the older half only); each must pass in BOTH halves.\n\nREJECTED (lost money on the newer half even at the lowest cost): Strict high tight flag -2.2%; 20 day high, quality version -1.0%; Fast mover continuation -1.1%; Undercut and reclaim -1.0%; Deep loser bought at the close, sold the next day -0.8%; Deep loser in an uptrend, bought at the close -0.5%; Most traded and strongest -0.6%; Bullish candle at the 50 day average in an uptrend -0.9%; Big news gap held for weeks -1.2%; Top-10% strength, tight base, breakout -1.2%; Earnings-style gap, short base, breakout -1.4%; Leader pullback continuation -0.7%; Volume build-up near the high -1.3%.\n\nNOT PROVEN: Tight base breakout\n  older half: 20 trades, 15% won, average -5.8%, profit factor 0.08\n  newer half: 17 trades, 6% won, average -5.3%, profit factor 0.07, stopped out 29%\n  too few trades (20 older, 17 newer; 20 each needed)\nNOT PROVEN: Holds up while the market falls\n  older half: 1182 trades, 36% won, average -0.9%, profit factor 0.66\n  newer half: 663 trades, 48% won, average +0.4%, profit factor 1.18, stopped out 13%\n  lost money in the older half; profit factor 1.18; no better than the S&P 500 over the same days; loses at higher costs (1.2% a trade); could still be luck after testing 16 ideas on the same years (false-discovery check)\nNOT PROVEN: Second day after a big up day\n  older half: 270 trades, 37% won, average -0.8%, profit factor 0.80\n  newer half: 226 trades, 38% won, average -0.3%, profit factor 0.93, stopped out 37%\n  lost money in the older half; average under zero at 0.8% cost; profit factor 0.93; no better than the S&P 500 over the same days; not clearly better than a random stock; loses at higher costs (1.2% a trade); could still be luck after testing 16 ideas on the same years (false-discovery check)\n\nMarket type check: no rule made money in rising markets in both halves.\n\nBuying a random stock for 10 days, newer half: 146842 trades, 43% won, average -0.5%, profit factor 0.85.\n\nEXIT TEST on the same quick-dip entries (24034 + 27229 trades)\n  current exit (5 day average or 5 days): older 24034 trades, 49% won, average -0.6%, profit factor 0.66 | newer 27229 trades, 51% won, average -0.5%, profit factor 0.75\n  take half at +1 daily move, let the rest run (trailing stop, up to 30 days): older 24034 trades, 50% won, average -1.0%, profit factor 0.63 | newer 27229 trades, 53% won, average -0.9%, profit factor 0.69\n  RESULT: KEEP THE CURRENT QUICK EXIT.\n\nNo new way passed. Nothing to act on. The lab repeats every Sunday as new days come in.\nNot tested here (no history to test on): Reddit or YouTube mentions plus a breakout, and news-tag rules. Those are scored forward instead (sources, movers journal).\nDaily prices only; fills at the open or the stated level are assumed. Research, not an order. Not financial advice, not a halal ruling."
